.TH CHTTPCLIENT_RESP_FREE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpclient_resp_free \- free a response and all its owned resources
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpclient.h>

void chttpclient_resp_free(chttpcli_response *resp);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Frees the response body buffer, the response headers map, and the
response struct itself.  Safe to call with NULL.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The _m_procs pointer inside the response is a non-owning reference to
the creating client's allocator.  When using a custom allocator, all
responses must be freed before the client that produced them is
destroyed.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpclient_do (3),
.BR chttpclient_resp_header (3)
